Google key attestation trust anchors and revocation list, used to check the hardware attestation of
the phone's bootloader and verified-boot state. Recorded in ADR 0015.

google-roots.pem
    Google's hardware attestation root certificates, copied from the Android Developers
    documentation, "Verify hardware-backed key pairs with key attestation"
    (https://developer.android.com/privacy-and-security/security-key-attestation). The site's
    licence page (https://developer.android.com/license) states that its documentation, including
    any code shown in it, is available under the Apache License 2.0
    (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).

revoked-serials.txt
    The serial numbers listed in Google's attestation certificate revocation status list
    (https://android.googleapis.com/attestation/status). Google publishes the list for anyone who
    verifies key attestation and states no licence for it. Only the serial numbers are kept: facts,
    used for the purpose the list is published for. ADR 0015's decision 12 asks for a legal review
    of this use before the first public release. That review has not happened yet: the list shipped
    in 0.1.0 to 0.1.2 without it, and the review is still open.

update.py
    The converter that produces both files: Apache-2.0, like the rest of this repository.
